<title>UK: BTR sells Dunlop Cox to Lear for 36 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BTR sells Dunlop Cox to Lear for 36 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British conglomerate BTR Plc said on Friday it had sold Dunlop Cox Ltd to U.S. group Lear Corp for 36 million stg cash.  </p>
<p>Dunlop, a maker of automotive seating mechanisms based in Nottingham, central England, had sales of 25 million stg in 1996.</p>
<p>Lear, based in Michigan, is one of the world's largest car seat makers.</p>
<p>BTR said the disposal would allow it to concentrate on further developing its global automotive business.</p>
<p>BTR's shares slipped 4.5p to 189 by 1330 GMT.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
